0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Z80
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-24).
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Four switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    EDITOR   1 = with the line editor built in (see the end of this file):
0000                             ;                 the spec's suggested standard. It goes with either setting
0000                             ;                 of the other two.
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     what the console escapes of "$" (/00bbIC8= /| /` /~) do:
0000                             ;             1 = send ANSI (VT100) sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = call the machine's own routines CONCLS, CONEOL, CONCUR and
0000                             ;                 CONAT (see the equates). The CP/M builds always send ANSI.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), Z80 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   1   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                EDITOR:   EQU   0   ; 1 = with the line editor
0000                ANSI:     EQU   0   ; 1 = the console escapes send ANSI sequences
0000                ANS:      EQU   ANSI+CPM-ANSI*CPM   ; (CP/M: always ANSI)
0000                EDGEN:    EQU   EDITOR*(1-CPM)   ; (the generic build with the editor)
0000                             ; (IF takes any value but 0 as true, so
0000                             ;  IF CHECKED+EDITOR means "either")
0000                TABP0:    EQU   EDGEN*(1-CHECKED)   ; (the build with its table in page zero)
0000                PTLATE:   EQU   1-CPM*EDITOR*(1-CHECKED)   ; (1: the table goes after psgn and pdec,
0000                             ;   not before them: wherever it doesn't cross a
0000                             ;   page. chktab.py says if it does)
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the Z80"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    HL'  return-stack pointer (the alternate HL). Entries are 2 bytes; the
0000                             ;         stack grows down. Only rpop and rpushn (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 08h  rpop    pop the return stack into DE
0000                             ;    RST 18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 18h and RST 30h never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing
0000                             ;  each of them does is POP DE to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block is written to work at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
0000                BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
0000                BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                                 ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
                    KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
                                 ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
                                 ;   (end the routine with OR A / RET).
                    CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
                                 ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE, HL and HL'.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-ANS   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the console escapes call these. All four must keep BC and
                                 ; HL', and all but CONAT also HL. They may change A, DE and the flags.
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Ch   ; /{  clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; /}  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF12h   ; /| and /`  show the cursor if A is not 0, hide
                                 ;     it if A = 0
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF15h   ; /~  the cursor to row HL, column DE, both
                                 ;     counted from 0. May change A, DE and HL
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
                    RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
                    DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
                    LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
                    PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
                    HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
                    BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDGEN   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0FF09h   ; where the editor's ^X goes
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    LEAVE:    EQU   0000h   ; the editor's ^X: warm boot
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   EDITOR   
                    EXIT:     EQU   edend   ; a program that ends goes back to the editor,
                    SKEND:    EQU   skend   ;   also when it ends inside skip
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0000                SKEND:    EQU   EXIT   
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine. (The wait
0000                             ; for a second Ctrl-C uses it too: 250 ms.)
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSAVE:    EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: return stack pointer, saved
0000                             ;   around machine code (and in the checked
0000                             ;   build the address "$" prints from);
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_';
0000                EDLN:     EQU   LET+3Ah   ;   the editor: the number of the line that ^E
0000                             ;   put in the input line (0: none)
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ; gap after z: a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0100                          .ORG   BASE   
0100                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset. (This byte, AFh, is also what an
0100                          ENDIF      ;     undefined word runs into: see e_hi.)
0100                          IF   1-EDGEN   
0100   31 FC 08               LD   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; 03  the IP
                              JR   st0   ; 06  (the rest of the startup is close by)
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                              JR   init   ; 04  (the rest of the startup is close by)
                              DW   0   ; 06  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   EDGEN   
                              XOR   A   ; 00  reset: no program yet. (This byte, AFh,
                              LD   (PROG),A   ;     is also what an undefined word runs
                              JP   init   ; 04  into in the checked build: see e_hi.)
                              NOP      ; 07  spare
0103                          ENDIF      
0103                          IF   CPM   
0103   C3 1E 06               JP   start   ; 03
0106   00 00                  DW   0   ; 06  spare
0108                          ENDIF      
0108                VECS:        
0108                             ; ---- RST 08h: rpop: pop the return stack into DE ---------------------------
0108   D9           RPOP:     EXX      ; 08
0109   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
010A   23                     INC   HL   
010B   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
010C   23                     INC   HL   
010D   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; across to the main registers
010E   D9                     EXX      
010F   D1                     POP   DE   
0110   C9                     RET      ; 10  (so RST 10h is not used)
0111                             ; ctl: the inner loop comes here for characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
0111   C6 21        CTL:      ADD   A,21h   ; 11  back to c; zero only for NUL
0113   20 1F                  JR   NZ,next0   ;     the rest are ignored
0115   C3 00 00     ENDPROG:   JP   EXIT   ;     the program has ended
0118                             ; ---- RST 18h: drop TOS, then next ------------------------------------------
0118   D1           RST18:    POP   DE   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0119   E1                     POP   HL   ;     new TOS = NOS
011A   18 15                  JR   nx   
011C   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   HL   ; 1C  "}" return stack to TOS
011D   CF                     RST   08h   
011E   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
011F   F7                     RST   30h   
0120                             ; ---- RST 20h: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) -------------------------------
0120   AF           NEG16:    XOR   A   ; 20
0121   95                     SUB   L   
0122   6F                     LD   L,A   
0123   9F                     SBC   A,A   
0124   94                     SUB   H   
0125   67                     LD   H,A   
0126   C9                     RET      
0127   00                     NOP      ; 27  spare
0128                             ; ---- RST 28h: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL, HL') ------------------------
0128                RST28:       
0128                          IFN   CPM   
                    PUTC:     JP   CONOUT   ; 28
0128                          ENDIF      
0128                          IF   CPM   
0128   C3 C6 04               JP   putc   ; 28
012B                          ENDIF      
012B   E9           JPHL:     JP   (HL)   ; 2B  (for the machine-code call)
012C   E3           H_TOR:    EX   (SP),HL   ; 2C  "{" TOS to the return stack: the new TOS
012D   C3 C9 01               JP   rpushn   ;     comes up, the old one goes across
0130                             ; ---- RST 30h: next character -----------------------------------------------
0130   D1           RST30:    POP   DE   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0131                NX:          
0131                          IF   CPM   
0131   C3 34 01               JP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0134                          ENDIF      
0134                VECEND:      
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0134                             ; 
0134                             ;    00h          end of program
0134                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0134                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0134                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0134                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0134                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0134                             ; =============================================================================
0134                NEXT0:       
0134                          IF   CHECKED   
0134   CD DF 04               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0137                          ENDIF      
0137   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0138   03                     INC   BC   
0139   D6 21                  SUB   21h   ; A = c - 21h
013B   38 D4                  JR   C,ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
013D   FE 0F                  CP   0Fh   
013F   38 25                  JR   C,punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0141   D6 0F                  SUB   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0143   FE 0A                  CP   0Ah   
0145   38 6C                  JR   C,digit   ; 30h-39h
0147   FE 11                  CP   11h   
0149   38 19                  JR   C,p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
014B   D6 11                  SUB   11h   ; A = c - 41h
014D   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   
014F   38 6E                  JR   C,upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0151   FE 20                  CP   20h   
0153   38 0D                  JR   C,p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0155   FE 3A                  CP   3Ah   
0157   38 60                  JR   C,lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
0159   FE 3E                  CP   3Eh   
015B                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JR   NC,next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
015B                          ENDIF      
015B                          IF   CHECKED   
015B   28 D7                  JR   Z,next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
015D   D2 0B 05               JP   NC,e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0160                          ENDIF      
0160   D6 1A                  SUB   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0162   D6 09        P5B:      SUB   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0164   C6 05        P3A:      ADD   A,5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
0166                .macro PTABLE,
0166                             ; 
0166                 DB      h_store & 0FFh  ; !
0166                 DB      h_str & 0FFh    ; "
0166                 DB      h_num & 0FFh    ; #
0166                 DB      h_print & 0FFh  ; $
0166                 DB      h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0166                 DB      h_and & 0FFh    ; &
0166                 DB      h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0166                 DB      h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0166                 DB      h_close & 0FFh  ; )
0166                 DB      h_mul & 0FFh    ; *
0166                 DB      h_add & 0FFh    ; +
0166                 DB      h_cfetch & 0FFh ; ,
0166                 DB      h_sub & 0FFh    ; -
0166                 DB      h_cstore & 0FFh ; .
0166                 DB      h_div & 0FFh    ; /
0166                 DB      h_dup & 0FFh    ; :
0166                 DB      h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0166                 DB      h_lt & 0FFh     ; <
0166                 DB      h_eq & 0FFh     ; =
0166                 DB      h_gt & 0FFh     ; >
0166                 DB      h_key & 0FFh    ; ?
0166                 DB      h_fetch & 0FFh  ; @
0166                 DB      h_def & 0FFh    ; [
0166                 DB      h_break & 0FFh  ; \
0166                 DB      h_ret & 0FFh    ; ]
0166                 DB      h_xor & 0FFh    ; ^
0166                 DB      h_alloc & 0FFh  ; _
0166                 DB      h_grave & 0FFh  ; `
0166                 DB      h_tor & 0FFh    ; {
0166                 DB      h_or & 0FFh     ; |
0166                 DB      h_fromr & 0FFh  ; }
0166                 DB      h_not & 0FFh    ; ~
0166                .endm
0166                 
0166                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
0166                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
0166   C6 66        PUNCT:    ADD   A,PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
0168   5F                     LD   E,A   
0169   16 04                  LD   D,PTAB / 256   ; (0 if the table is in page zero)
016B   FE 7C                  CP   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
016D   1A                     LD   A,(DE)   
016E   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
016F                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-TABP0)   
                              LD   D,0   
016F                          ENDIF      
016F                          IFN   CPM   
                              RL   D   ; its page: 0 + carry
016F                          ENDIF      
016F                          IF   CPM   
016F   16 01                  LD   D,1   
0171   30 01                  JR   NC,pu1   
0173   14                     INC   D   ; its page: 1 + carry
0174                PU1:         
0174                          ENDIF      
0174   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0175   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
0176                             ; The rest of the startup: here so that the generic reset code can reach it
0176                             ; with JR. st0: find the program's NUL; the heap starts after it.
0176                             ; (The editor build has its own copy of this, next to the editor.)
0176                             ; A checked build first clears the lower half of the letter page (A = 0):
0176                             ; every variable starts at 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an
0176                             ; undefined word is caught at (see e_hi), and no key is held back.
0176                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)*CHECKED   
                    INIT:     LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
                              LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    ST0:      LD   H,B   
                              LD   L,C   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
0176                          ENDIF      
0176                          IF   1-EDITOR   
0176   22 7C 09     ST2:      LD   (HEAP),HL   
0179                          ENDIF      
0179                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
0179   E7                     RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
017A   22 38 09               LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*(1-CPM)   
                              LD   H,A   ; (A = 0) no key is held, and the break key
                              LD   L,A   ;   is on (the checked build has cleared
017D                          ENDIF      ;   these)
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)*CPM   
                              LD   HL,0   
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   
017D                          ENDIF      
017D                          IF   1-EDITOR   
017D   D9                     EXX      
017E   21 E0 07               LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
0181   D9                     EXX      
0182   F7                     RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
0183                          ENDIF      
0183                             ; In the unchecked generic editor build the table is here, in the first
0183                             ; page, which saves loading D twice. (The other builds have no room for it
0183                             ; here: theirs is further down.)
0183                          IF   TABP0   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
0183                          ENDIF      
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0183                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.) The machine-code call, exec,
0183                             ;  is here too: it belongs to "`" and makes the page come out right.
0183                             ; =============================================================================
0183   D1           H_XOR:    POP   DE   
0184   7C                     LD   A,H   
0185   AA                     XOR   D   
0186   67                     LD   H,A   
0187   7D                     LD   A,L   
0188   AB                     XOR   E   
0189   6F                     LD   L,A   
018A   F7                     RST   30h   
018B   D1           H_OR:     POP   DE   
018C   7C                     LD   A,H   
018D   B2                     OR   D   
018E   67                     LD   H,A   
018F   7D                     LD   A,L   
0190   B3                     OR   E   
0191   6F                     LD   L,A   
0192   F7                     RST   30h   
0193   E7           H_NOT:    RST   20h   ; ~x = -x - 1
0194   2B                     DEC   HL   
0195   F7                     RST   30h   
0196                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0196                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0196   ED 5B 7C 09  H_ALLOC:   LD   DE,(HEAP)   
019A                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
019A   7C                     LD   A,H   ; the count's sign, for chkhp
019B                          ENDIF      
019B   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; the new top
019C                          IF   CHECKED   
019C   CD 15 05               CALL   chkhp   
019F                          ENDIF      
019F   22 7C 09               LD   (HEAP),HL   
01A2   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
01A3   F7                     RST   30h   
01A4   D9           EXEC:     EXX      
01A5   22 34 09               LD   (RSAVE),HL   ; machine code may change the alternates
01A8   D9                     EXX      
01A9   CD 2B 01               CALL   jphl   
01AC   D9                     EXX      
01AD   2A 34 09               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
01B0   D9                     EXX      
01B1   E1                     POP   HL   
01B2   F7                     RST   30h   
01B3                             ; ---- the letters and digits (here, in the middle, so that the inner loop's
01B3                             ; ---- short jumps reach them, and the handlers after them reach rpushn) ------
01B3                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
01B3   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   HL   
01B4   0B                     DEC   BC   
01B5   CD D6 03               CALL   rdnum   
01B8   F7                     RST   30h   
01B9                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
01B9   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   HL   
01BA   87                     ADD   A,A   
01BB   6F                     LD   L,A   
01BC   26 09                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
01BE   F7                     RST   30h   
01BF                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
01BF                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
01BF   C5           UPPER:    PUSH   BC   ; the return address, for rpushn
01C0   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; park TOS
01C1   87                     ADD   A,A   
01C2   6F                     LD   L,A   
01C3   26 09                  LD   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
01C5   4E                     LD   C,(HL)   
01C6   2C                     INC   L   
01C7   46                     LD   B,(HL)   ; IP = the word's body
01C8   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; TOS back, and fall into rpushn
01C9                             ; rpushn: move the top cell of the data stack (in memory) to the return
01C9                             ; stack, then next. Everything that pushes the return stack ends here.
01C9                             ; 
01C9                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
01C9                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: B', which nothing else
01C9                             ; uses, counts them. Reading the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call
01C9                             ; under CP/M), and this way it costs a loop four bytes and 14 T-states.
01C9                             ; (DEC B, not DJNZ: its zero flag lasts through the EXX, so one EXX serves
01C9                             ; both ways out.)
01C9   D9           RPUSHN:   EXX      
01CA   D1                     POP   DE   
01CB   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CC   72                     LD   (HL),D   
01CD   2B                     DEC   HL   
01CE   73                     LD   (HL),E   
01CF   05                     DEC   B   
01D0   D9                     EXX      
01D1   CC 86 04               CALL   Z,pollk   
01D4   F7                     RST   30h   
01D5                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
01D5                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
01D5                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
01D5                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
01D5                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
01D5                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
01D5                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
01D5   CD 3A 04     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
01D8   30 CA                  JR   NC,exec   
01DA   77           HX1:      LD   (HL),A   ; the high digit goes in first ...
01DB   CD 3A 04               CALL   hexc   
01DE   30 08                  JR   NC,hx2   ; odd digit: consumed, and the RET below
01E0   ED 6F                  RLD      ;   overwrites it
01E2   23                     INC   HL   ; ... and RLD shifts it up under the low one
01E3   CD 3A 04               CALL   hexc   
01E6   38 F2                  JR   C,hx1   
01E8   36 C9        HX2:      LD   (HL),0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
01EA   F7                     RST   30h   
01EB                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
01EB                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
01EB                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
01EB                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
01EB                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
01EB                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it.
01EB   CF           H_RET:    RST   08h   
01EC   42                     LD   B,D   
01ED   4B                     LD   C,E   
01EE   F7           BRK1:     RST   30h   
01EF                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
01EF                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
01EF   7C           H_BREAK:   LD   A,H   
01F0   B5                     OR   L   
01F1   E1                     POP   HL   
01F2   28 FA                  JR   Z,brk1   
01F4   CD FD 03               CALL   skip   
01F7   B7                     OR   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
01F8   20 F1                  JR   NZ,h_ret   
01FA   CF           RDROP:    RST   08h   
01FB   F7                     RST   30h   
01FC                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
01FC                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
01FC                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
01FC                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
01FC                             ; checked build stops on it.)
01FC   0A           H_DEF:    LD   A,(BC)   
01FD   03                     INC   BC   
01FE   D6 41                  SUB   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
0200   5F                     LD   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
0201   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   ; fold case
0203   FE 1A                  CP   26   
0205   30 0B                  JR   NC,def2   ; not a letter
0207   CB 23                  SLA   E   
0209   16 09                  LD   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
020B   79                     LD   A,C   
020C   12                     LD   (DE),A   
020D   1C                     INC   E   
020E   78                     LD   A,B   
020F   12                     LD   (DE),A   
0210   18 09                  JR   skipnx   
0212                DEF2:        
0212                          IF   CHECKED   
0212   7B                     LD   A,E   
0213   FE DF                  CP   " "-"A"+256   
0215   C2 5D 05               JP   NZ,e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0218                          ENDIF      
0218   E5                     PUSH   HL   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0219   60                     LD   H,B   
021A   69                     LD   L,C   
021B                SKIPNX:      
021B                          IF   CHECKED   
021B   0B                     DEC   BC   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
021C                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
021C   CD FD 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
021F   F7                     RST   30h   
0220   5E           H_FETCH:   LD   E,(HL)   ; "@"
0221   23                     INC   HL   
0222   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
0223   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0224   F7                     RST   30h   
0225                             ; =============================================================================
0225                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0225                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it), so its long tail may run past that
0225                             ;  page.
0225                             ; =============================================================================
0225                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0225                             ; the matching ")".
0225   7C           H_OPEN:   LD   A,H   
0226   B5                     OR   L   
0227   E1                     POP   HL   
0228   28 F2                  JR   Z,skipo   
022A   C5                     PUSH   BC   ; the block starts at the IP
022B   18 9C                  JR   rpushn   
022D                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
022D                             ; drops it and carries on.
022D   7C           H_CLOSE:   LD   A,H   
022E   B5                     OR   L   
022F   E1                     POP   HL   
0230   28 C8                  JR   Z,rdrop   
0232   CF                     RST   08h   ; pop the block start ...
0233   42                     LD   B,D   
0234   4B                     LD   C,E   
0235   C5                     PUSH   BC   
0236   18 91                  JR   rpushn   ; ... and push it back
0238                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0238                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0238   0A           H_SUB:    LD   A,(BC)   
0239   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
023B   FE 0A                  CP   10   
023D   38 04                  JR   C,negnum   
023F   E7                     RST   20h   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0240   D1           H_ADD:    POP   DE   
0241   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0242   F7                     RST   30h   
0243   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   HL   ; a negative number: read it, negate it
0244   CD D6 03               CALL   rdnum   
0247   E7                     RST   20h   
0248   F7                     RST   30h   
0249   D1           H_AND:    POP   DE   
024A   7C                     LD   A,H   
024B   A2                     AND   D   
024C   67                     LD   H,A   
024D   7D                     LD   A,L   
024E   A3                     AND   E   
024F   6F                     LD   L,A   
0250   F7                     RST   30h   
0251                             ; Signed compares. Both are "HL < DE" for the right pair: "<" swaps the two
0251                             ; cells first. Flipping both sign bits turns a signed compare into an
0251                             ; unsigned one (and XOR clears the carry for SBC); SBC HL,HL then turns the
0251                             ; carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
0251   E3           H_LT:     EX   (SP),HL   ; a < b: HL = a, and b is popped next
0252   D1           H_GT:     POP   DE   ; a > b  is  b < a: HL = b, DE = a
0253   7C                     LD   A,H   
0254   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
0256   67                     LD   H,A   
0257   7A                     LD   A,D   
0258   EE 80                  XOR   80h   
025A   57                     LD   D,A   
025B   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry if HL < DE
025D   ED 62        TF:       SBC   HL,HL   ; carry -> -1 or 0
025F   F7                     RST   30h   
0260   D1           H_EQ:     POP   DE   
0261   B7                     OR   A   
0262   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
0264   7C                     LD   A,H   
0265   B5                     OR   L   
0266   FE 01                  CP   1   ; carry only if a - b = 0
0268   18 F3                  JR   tf   
026A                             ; "*": shift-and-add, 16 rounds; only the low 16 bits are kept. The
026A                             ; multiplier shifts up through A:C.
026A   D1           H_MUL:    POP   DE   ; DE = multiplicand
026B   C5                     PUSH   BC   
026C   7C                     LD   A,H   
026D   4D                     LD   C,L   ; A:C = multiplier
026E   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
0271   06 10                  LD   B,16   
0273   29           MUL1:     ADD   HL,HL   
0274   CB 21                  SLA   C   
0276   17                     RLA      
0277   30 01                  JR   NC,mul2   
0279   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
027A   10 F7        MUL2:     DJNZ   mul1   
027C   C1                     POP   BC   
027D   F7                     RST   30h   
027E                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
027E                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
027E                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
027E                             ; stops on it.
027E                H_DIV:       
027E                          IF   CHECKED   
027E   7C                     LD   A,H   
027F   B5                     OR   L   
0280   CA 5A 05               JP   Z,e_zero   
0283                          ENDIF      
0283   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = a, HL = b
0284   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; a, for r's sign
0285   7A                     LD   A,D   
0286   AC                     XOR   H   
0287   F5                     PUSH   AF   ; S flag = sign of q
0288   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
028A   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |b|
028D   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
028E   CB 7C                  BIT   7,H   
0290   C4 20 01               CALL   NZ,neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
0293   CD AE 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, DE = r
0296   F1                     POP   AF   
0297   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; q's sign
029A   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; HL = r, DE = q
029B   F1                     POP   AF   ; A = a's high byte
029C   B7                     OR   A   
029D   FC 20 01               CALL   M,neg16   ; r's sign
02A0   D5                     PUSH   DE   ; q under r
02A1   F7                     RST   30h   
02A2                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
02A2   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   HL   ; ":"
02A3   F7                     RST   30h   
02A4   E3           H_SWAP:   EX   (SP),HL   ; "%"
02A5   F7                     RST   30h   
02A6                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
02A6                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
02A6                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
02A6                          IF   CHECKED   
02A6   CD 32 05               CALL   chkst   
02A9                          ENDIF      
02A9   D1                     POP   DE   
02AA   73                     LD   (HL),E   
02AB   DF           H_DROP:   RST   18h   ; ";" is this one byte
02AC                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
02AC                          IF   CHECKED   
02AC   CD 32 05               CALL   chkst   
02AF                          ENDIF      
02AF   D1                     POP   DE   
02B0   73                     LD   (HL),E   
02B1   23                     INC   HL   
02B2   72                     LD   (HL),D   
02B3   DF                     RST   18h   
02B4                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
02B4                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
02B4   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   HL   
02B5   60                     LD   H,B   
02B6   69                     LD   L,C   
02B7   CD EC 03               CALL   skipstr   
02BA                          IF   CHECKED   
02BA   B7                     OR   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
02BB   CA 52 05               JP   Z,e_quote   
02BE                          ENDIF      
02BE   F7                     RST   30h   
02BF                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
02BF                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
02BF                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, and / then DEL gives "?"; "/',
02BF                             ; '"' and '?' have no bit 6, so //, /" and /? give themselves).
02BF                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   Z,pr9   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   NZ,pr1   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   60h   
                              JR   C,pr0   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   C,pesc   
                    PR0:      AND   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   h_print   
                    PRLOOP:   EQU   h_print   ; (where the escapes go back to)
                    PRAGAIN:   EQU   h_print   ; (and where /~ goes back to)
02BF                          ENDIF      
02BF                          IF   CHECKED   
02BF                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
02BF                             ; report uses too. The address is kept meanwhile, for a report: it shows
02BF                             ; the stack as it was before the "$". /~ comes back to hp1.)
02BF   22 34 09     H_PRINT:   LD   (RSAVE),HL   
02C2   CD 18 03     HP1:      CALL   prstr   
02C5   DF                     RST   18h   
02C6                          ENDIF      
02C6   7D           H_EMIT:   LD   A,L   ; "'"
02C7   EF                     RST   28h   
02C8   DF           PR9:      RST   18h   
02C9                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
02C9   CD 4C 04     H_NUM:    CALL   psgn   
02CC   DF                     RST   18h   
02CD                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
02CD                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
02CD                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
02CD                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
02CD                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
02CD   CB 7C        H_KEY:    BIT   7,H   
02CF   20 19                  JR   NZ,line   
02D1   1E 28        KT1:      LD   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
02D3   CD B4 04     KT2:      CALL   getk   
02D6   20 0E                  JR   NZ,kt3   
02D8   1D                     DEC   E   
02D9   20 F8                  JR   NZ,kt2   
02DB   7C                     LD   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
02DC   B5                     OR   L   
02DD   28 F2                  JR   Z,kt1   
02DF   2B                     DEC   HL   
02E0   7C                     LD   A,H   
02E1   B5                     OR   L   
02E2   20 ED                  JR   NZ,kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
02E4   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CP n: steps over the one byte of ",")
02E5   7E           H_CFETCH:   LD   A,(HL)   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
02E6   6F           KT3:      LD   L,A   
02E7   26 00                  LD   H,0   
02E9   F7                     RST   30h   
02EA                             ; Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as it
02EA                             ; is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
02EA                             ; echoed until the line is full. (CP/M too: getk reads through BDOS
02EA                             ; 6.) The line buffer starts at offset 80h of its page, so L alone
02EA                             ; is the place in the line: D holds the L of a full line.
02EA   11 7F 00     LINE:     LD   DE,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
02ED   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
02EE   9F                     SBC   A,A   
02EF   A5                     AND   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
02F0   2F                     CPL      
02F1   57                     LD   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
02F2                             ;   at most
02F2   21 80 09               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
02F5   CD B4 04     LN2:      CALL   getk   
02F8   28 FB                  JR   Z,ln2   
02FA   FE 0D                  CP   13   
02FC   28 16                  JR   Z,ln5   
02FE   FE 08                  CP   8   
0300   28 0B                  JR   Z,ln4   
0302   5F                     LD   E,A   
0303   7D                     LD   A,L   
0304   BA                     CP   D   
0305   28 EE                  JR   Z,ln2   ; full
0307   73                     LD   (HL),E   
0308   2C                     INC   L   
0309   7B                     LD   A,E   
030A   EF           LN3:      RST   28h   
030B   18 E8                  JR   ln2   
030D   2D           LN4:      DEC   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
030E   FA 0A 03               JP   M,ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
0311   2C                     INC   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0312   18 E1                  JR   ln2   
0314   77           LN5:      LD   (HL),A   ; the CR
0315   2E 80                  LD   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0317   F7                     RST   30h   
0318                             ; =============================================================================
0318                             ;  More routines (no handler starts past this point)
0318                             ; =============================================================================
0318                          IF   CHECKED   
0318                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
0318                             ; "$", and the texts of the report). A NUL first is an error: Q.
0318   7E           PRSTR:    LD   A,(HL)   
0319   23                     INC   HL   
031A   FE 22                  CP   22h   
031C   C8                     RET   Z   
031D   B7                     OR   A   
031E   CA 48 05               JP   Z,e_dollar   
0321   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
0323   20 0C                  JR   NZ,prs1   
0325   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0326   23                     INC   HL   
0327   FE 60                  CP   60h   
0329   38 04                  JR   C,prs0   
032B   FE 7F                  CP   7Fh   
032D   38 11                  JR   C,pesc   
032F   E6 BF        PRS0:     AND   0BFh   
0331   EF           PRS1:     RST   28h   
0332   18 E4                  JR   prstr   
0334                PRLOOP:   EQU   prstr   ; (where the escapes go back to)
0334                PRAGAIN:   EQU   hp1   ; (and where /~ goes back to)
0334                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
0334                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
0334   3E 0D        PNL:      LD   A,13   
0336   EF                     RST   28h   
0337   3E 0A                  LD   A,10   
0339   EF                     RST   28h   
033A   E3           PMSG:     EX   (SP),HL   
033B   CD 18 03               CALL   prstr   
033E   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   
033F   C9                     RET      
0340                          ENDIF      
0340                             ; pesc: the escapes of "$". A = the character after the "/", 60h to 7Eh, and
0340                             ; HL points past it. Each goes back into the loop that prints the string
0340                             ; (PRLOOP), but /~ has the stack to see to, and goes back by PRAGAIN.
0340                             ;    /a-/z   print the variable, as "#" does
0340                             ;    /{      clear the screen, the cursor to the top left
0340                             ;    /}      clear from the cursor to the end of the line
0340                             ;    /|  /`  show the cursor, hide it
0340                             ;    /~      ( row col -- ) the cursor to that row and column, from 0
0340   FE 7E        PESC:     CP   7Eh   
0342   28 1C                  JR   Z,pat   
0344   11 18 03               LD   DE,PRLOOP   ; the others return into the loop
0347   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0348   D6 7B                  SUB   7Bh   ; 00bbIDAsIHwgMSwg 2, and no borrow
034A   30 47                  JR   NC,pcon   
034C   C6 1A                  ADD   A,1Ah   ; a-z: 0-25, and a carry; `: FFh, and none
034E   30 35                  JR   NC,phide   
0350   87                     ADD   A,A   ; the variable's cell
0351   C6 40                  ADD   A,40h   
0353   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0354   6F                     LD   L,A   
0355   26 09                  LD   H,LETPAGE   
0357   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0358   2C                     INC   L   
0359   66                     LD   H,(HL)   
035A   6F                     LD   L,A   
035B   CD 4C 04               CALL   psgn   
035E   E1                     POP   HL   
035F   C9                     RET      
0360                             ; /~ ( row col addr -- ): the two cells under the string's address go. In
0360                             ; the checked build "$" is the routine prstr: its own return address goes
0360                             ; first, and hp1 calls it again afterwards. There each /~ first looks that
0360                             ; its two cells are there, and is s if not, before it prints anything.
0360                PAT:         
0360                          IF   CHECKED   
0360   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; the text pointer over prstr's return address
0361   21 0A F7               LD   HL,(6-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; a carry: the two cells aren't there
0364   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
0365   DA 04 05               JP   C,e_under   
0368   E1                     POP   HL   
0369                          ENDIF      
0369   D1                     POP   DE   ; DE = the column
036A   E3                     EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the row; the text pointer is kept
036B                          IF   1-ANS   
                              CALL   CONAT   
                              POP   HL   
                              JP   PRAGAIN   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's routines do the rest.
                    PCON:     JP   Z,CONCLS   ; /{
                              CP   2   
                              JP   Z,CONEOL   ; /}
                              DB   0FEh   ; /|  (CP n steps over the XOR: A = 1, show)
                    PHIDE:    XOR   A   ; /`  (A = 0: hide)
                              JP   CONCUR   
036B                          ENDIF      
036B                          IF   ANS   
036B   D5                     PUSH   DE   
036C   CD A7 03               CALL   csi   ; ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H (ANSI counts from 1)
036F   23                     INC   HL   
0370   CD 54 04               CALL   pdec   
0373   3E 3B                  LD   A,";"   
0375   EF                     RST   28h   
0376   E1                     POP   HL   
0377   23                     INC   HL   
0378   CD 54 04               CALL   pdec   
037B   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
037D   EF                     RST   28h   
037E   E1                     POP   HL   
037F   C3 C2 02               JP   PRAGAIN   
0382                             ; With ANSI = 1 they are sequences. The carry is clear on the way in.
0382   1E 68        PSHOW:    LD   E,"h"   ; /|  ESC [ ? 2 5 h
0384   DA                     DB   0DAh   ; (JP C,nn: with no carry it steps over two bytes)
0385   1E 6C        PHIDE:    LD   E,"l"   ; /`  ESC [ ? 2 5 l
0387                          ENDIF      
0387                          IF   ANS*CHECKED   
0387                             ; (The checked build prints the fixed parts with pmsg, which it has for the
0387                             ; report: shorter than a character at a time.)
0387   CD 3A 03               CALL   pmsg   
038A   1B 5B 3F 32 35 22      DB   27,"[?25",22h   
0390   7B           PSE:      LD   A,E   ; then E
0391   EF                     RST   28h   
0392   C9                     RET      
0393                             ; pcon: /00bbIC98IC8=, with A = 0, 1, 2. /{ runs on into cse.
0393   3D           PCON:     DEC   A   
0394   28 EC                  JR   Z,pshow   ; /|
0396   1E 4B                  LD   E,"K"   
0398   F2 A2 03               JP   P,cse   ; /}  ESC [ K
039B   1E 48                  LD   E,"H"   ; /{  ESC [ H ESC [ J
039D   CD A2 03               CALL   cse   
03A0   1E 4A                  LD   E,"J"   ; (on into cse)
03A2                             ; cse: ESC [ and then E. csi: ESC [. Both keep HL.
03A2   CD A7 03     CSE:      CALL   csi   
03A5   18 E9                  JR   pse   
03A7   CD 3A 03     CSI:      CALL   pmsg   
03AA   1B 5B 22               DB   27,"[",22h   
03AD   C9                     RET      
03AE                          ENDIF      
03AE                          IF   ANS*(1-CHECKED)   
                              LD   A,"?"   
                              CALL   csia   
                              LD   A,"2"   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,"5"   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,E   
                              RST   28h   
                              RET      
                                 ; pcon: /00bbIC98IC8=, with A = 0, 1, 2. /{ runs on into csia.
                    PCON:     DEC   A   
                              JR   Z,pshow   ; /|
                              LD   A,"K"   
                              JP   P,csia   ; /}  ESC [ K
                              LD   A,"H"   ; /{  ESC [ H ESC [ J
                              CALL   csia   
                              LD   A,"J"   ; (on into csia)
                                 ; csia: ESC [ and then A. csi: ESC [, keeping A.
                    CSIA:     CALL   csi   
                              RST   28h   
                              RET      
                    CSI:      PUSH   AF   
                              LD   A,27   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,"["   
                              RST   28h   
                              POP   AF   
                              RET      
03AE                          ENDIF      
03AE                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, DE = remainder.
03AE                             ; Uses A; keeps BC (the IP) itself. The dividend shifts up through A:C while
03AE                             ; the quotient bits arrive at the bottom of C.
03AE                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
03AE   7B           UDIV:     LD   A,E   
03AF   EE 02                  XOR   2   
03B1   B2                     OR   D   
03B2   20 07                  JR   NZ,udv0   
03B4   CB 3C                  SRL   H   
03B6   CB 1D                  RR   L   ; the quotient
03B8   8F                     ADC   A,A   
03B9   5F                     LD   E,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out (D is 0)
03BA   C9                     RET      
03BB   C5           UDV0:     PUSH   BC   
03BC   7C                     LD   A,H   
03BD   4D                     LD   C,L   
03BE   21 00 00               LD   HL,0   
03C1   06 10                  LD   B,16   
03C3   CB 21        UDV1:     SLA   C   
03C5   17                     RLA      
03C6   ED 6A                  ADC   HL,HL   
03C8   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   ; carry is clear here: the remainder
03CA   30 02                  JR   NC,udv2   ;   always fits in 16 bits
03CC   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; too much: put it back, and cancel the
03CD   0D                     DEC   C   ;   INC below
03CE   0C           UDV2:     INC   C   ; a quotient bit
03CF   10 F2                  DJNZ   udv1   
03D1   EB                     EX   DE,HL   ; DE = remainder
03D2   67                     LD   H,A   
03D3   69                     LD   L,C   ; HL = quotient
03D4   C1                     POP   BC   
03D5   C9                     RET      
03D6                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
03D6                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
03D6   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LD   HL,0   
03D9   0A           RDN1:     LD   A,(BC)   
03DA   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
03DC   FE 0A                  CP   10   
03DE   D0                     RET   NC   
03DF   03                     INC   BC   
03E0   54                     LD   D,H   
03E1   5D                     LD   E,L   
03E2   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
03E3   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
03E4   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
03E5   29                     ADD   HL,HL   ; HL * 10
03E6   5F                     LD   E,A   
03E7   16 00                  LD   D,0   
03E9   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
03EA   18 ED                  JR   rdn1   
03EC                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
03EC                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
03EC                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INC   BC   
                    SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
                              INC   BC   
                              CP   "/"   
                              JR   Z,ss0   
                              CP   22h   
                              JR   NZ,skipstr   
                              RET      
03EC                          ENDIF      
03EC                          IF   CHECKED   
03EC                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
03EC                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
03EC   0A           SKIPSTR:   LD   A,(BC)   
03ED   B7                     OR   A   
03EE   C8                     RET   Z   
03EF   03                     INC   BC   
03F0   FE 22                  CP   22h   
03F2   C8                     RET   Z   
03F3   FE 2F                  CP   "/"   
03F5   20 F5                  JR   NZ,skipstr   
03F7   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   ; the escaped character
03F8   B7                     OR   A   
03F9   C8                     RET   Z   
03FA   03                     INC   BC   
03FB   18 EF                  JR   skipstr   
03FD                          ENDIF      
03FD                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
03FD                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
03FD                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
03FD                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
03FD                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
03FD                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INC that an opener comes back to.
03FD                             ; 
03FD                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
03FD                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
03FD                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
03FD                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. IX keeps the
03FD                             ; place where the skip started, for the report.
03FD                SKIP:        
03FD                          IF   CHECKED   
03FD   C5                     PUSH   BC   
03FE   DD E1                  POP   IX   
0400   0B                     DEC   BC   
0401   0A                     LD   A,(BC)   
0402   03                     INC   BC   
0403   5F                     LD   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
0404                          ENDIF      
0404   16 00                  LD   D,0   
0406   14           SK3:      INC   D   ; an opener: one deeper
0407   0A           SK1:      LD   A,(BC)   
0408                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INC   BC   
                              OR   A   
                              JP   Z,SKEND   ; (the end of the program)
0408                          ENDIF      
0408                          IF   CHECKED   
0408   B7                     OR   A   
0409   28 22                  JR   Z,sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
040B   03                     INC   BC   
040C                          ENDIF      
040C   FE 22                  CP   22h   
040E   CC EC 03               CALL   Z,skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
0411   D6 28                  SUB   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
0413   28 F1                  JR   Z,sk3   
0415   3D                     DEC   A   ; ")"
0416   28 08                  JR   Z,sk4   
0418   D6 32                  SUB   "["-")"   
041A   28 EA                  JR   Z,sk3   
041C   FE 02                  CP   "]"-"["   
041E   20 E7                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0420   15           SK4:      DEC   D   
0421                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RET   Z   ; the closer at this level
                              JR   sk1   
0421                          ENDIF      
0421                          IF   CHECKED   
0421   20 E4                  JR   NZ,sk1   
0423   57                     LD   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
0424   AB                     XOR   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
0425   E6 06                  AND   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
0427   FE 02                  CP   2   ;   closer, and only then
0429   7A                     LD   A,D   
042A   C0                     RET   NZ   
042B   18 05                  JR   sk7   
042D   CB 53        SK6:      BIT   2,E   ; the text ran out:
042F   C2 00 00               JP   NZ,SKEND   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
0432   DD E5        SK7:      PUSH   IX   ; N. The place is the opener
0434   C1                     POP   BC   
0435   3E 4E                  LD   A,"N"   
0437   C3 45 05               JP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
043A                          ENDIF      
043A                             ; =============================================================================
043A                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order
043A                             ;  (the table itself is the macro PTABLE, defined above the dispatcher).
043A                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
043A                             ; =============================================================================
043A                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
043A                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
043A                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
043A                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
043A                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
043A                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
043A                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
043A                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
043A                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
043A                          IF   (1-TABP0)*(1-PTLATE)   
                    PTAB:        
                              ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
                              DB   h_store & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_str & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_num & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_print & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_and & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_open & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_close & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_add & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_div & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_key & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_def & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_break & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_or & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
                              DB   h_not & 0FFh   
                    PTABEND:      
043A                          ENDIF      
043A                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
043A                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
043A                             ; return with the carry clear.
043A   0A           HEXC:     LD   A,(BC)   
043B   D6 30                  SUB   "0"   
043D   FE 0A                  CP   10   
043F   38 09                  JR   C,hc1   
0441   E6 DF                  AND   0DFh   
0443   D6 11                  SUB   11h   
0445   FE 06                  CP   6   
0447   D0                     RET   NC   
0448   D6 F6                  SUB   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
044A   03           HC1:      INC   BC   
044B   C9                     RET      
044C                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Keeps BC.
044C   CB 7C        PSGN:     BIT   7,H   
044E   28 04                  JR   Z,pdec   
0450   3E 2D                  LD   A,"-"   
0452   EF                     RST   28h   
0453   E7                     RST   20h   
0454                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
0454                             ; Keeps BC.
0454   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LD   DE,10   
0457   CD AE 03               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, E = the last digit
045A   7B                     LD   A,E   
045B   F5                     PUSH   AF   
045C   7C                     LD   A,H   
045D   B5                     OR   L   
045E   C4 54 04               CALL   NZ,pdec   
0461   F1                     POP   AF   
0462   C6 30                  ADD   A,"0"   
0464   EF                     RST   28h   
0465   C9                     RET      
0466                             ; (The table goes here instead in the builds where, before psgn, it would
0466                             ; cross a page: PTLATE.)
0466                          IF   (1-TABP0)*PTLATE   
0466                PTAB:        
0466                          ;*Macro unroll:  PTABLE
0466   AC                     DB   h_store & 0FFh   
0467   B4                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   
0468   C9                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   
0469   BF                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   
046A   A4                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   
046B   49                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   
046C   C6                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   
046D   25                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   
046E   2D                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   
046F   6A                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   
0470   40                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   
0471   E5                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   
0472   38                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   
0473   A6                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   
0474   7E                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   
0475   A2                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   
0476   AB                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   
0477   51                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   
0478   60                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   
0479   52                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   
047A   CD                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   
047B   20                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   
047C   FC                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   
047D   EF                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   
047E   EB                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   
047F   83                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   
0480   96                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   
0481   D5                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   
0482   2C                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   
0483   8B                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   
0484   1C                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   
0485   93                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   
0486                PTABEND:      
0486                          ENDIF      
0486                             ; =============================================================================
0486                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
0486                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
0486                             ;  (RST 28h) prints A. Both keep BC, DE, HL and HL'. In the generic build
0486                             ;  they are the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
0486                             ; 
0486                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
0486                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
0486                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
0486                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
0486                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
0486                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
0486                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
0486                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
0486                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
0486                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
0486                             ;  data stack.
0486                             ; =============================================================================
0486                          IFN   CPM   
                    RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
0486                          ENDIF      
0486                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushn).
0486   CD C4 04     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
0489   C8                     RET   Z   ; no key
048A   32 7A 09               LD   (KEYBUF),A   ; held for the next "?"
048D   FE 03        PK1:      CP   3   ; (getk joins here)
048F   C0                     RET   NZ   
0490                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
0490                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
0490                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
0490                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
0490   3A 7B 09     CTLC:     LD   A,(BRKOFF)   
0493   B7                     OR   A   
0494   CA 43 05     CT0:      JP   Z,brk   
0497   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0498   11 10 27               LD   DE,250*MSLOOP   
049B   CD C4 04     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
049E   20 05                  JR   NZ,ct2   
04A0   1B                     DEC   DE   
04A1   7A                     LD   A,D   
04A2   B3                     OR   E   
04A3   20 F6                  JR   NZ,ct1   
04A5   D1           CT2:      POP   DE   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
04A6   FE 03                  CP   3   
04A8   28 EA                  JR   Z,ct0   ; (the zero flag takes the JP there)
04AA   B7                     OR   A   
04AB   28 03                  JR   Z,ct3   
04AD   32 7A 09               LD   (KEYBUF),A   
04B0   3E 03        CT3:      LD   A,3   
04B2   B7                     OR   A   
04B3   C9                     RET      
04B4                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
04B4   E5           GETK:     PUSH   HL   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
04B5   21 7A 09               LD   HL,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
04B8   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
04B9   36 00                  LD   (HL),0   
04BB   E1                     POP   HL   
04BC   B7                     OR   A   
04BD   C0                     RET   NZ   
04BE   CD C4 04               CALL   rawk   
04C1   C8                     RET   Z   
04C2   18 C9                  JR   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
04C4                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-EDITOR)   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word
04C4                          ENDIF      ;   (with the editor, both stacks are cleared);
04C4                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*EDITOR   
                    BRK:      EQU   edit0   
04C4                          ENDIF      
04C4                          IF   CHECKED   
04C4                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
04C4                          ENDIF      
04C4                          IF   CPM   
04C4   3E FF        RAWK:     LD   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
04C6                             ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
04C6                             ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
04C6   D5           PUTC:     PUSH   DE   
04C7   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04C8   5F                     LD   E,A   
04C9   3E 06                  LD   A,6   
04CB   CD D2 04               CALL   bdosx   
04CE   E1                     POP   HL   
04CF   D1                     POP   DE   
04D0   B7                     OR   A   ; (for getk)
04D1   C9                     RET      
04D2                             ; bdosx: call BDOS function A with DE, keeping BC and HL'
04D2   C5           BDOSX:    PUSH   BC   
04D3   D9                     EXX      
04D4   E5                     PUSH   HL   
04D5   D9                     EXX      
04D6   4F                     LD   C,A   
04D7   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
04DA   D9                     EXX      
04DB   E1                     POP   HL   
04DC   D9                     EXX      
04DD   C1                     POP   BC   
04DE   C9                     RET      
04DF                          ENDIF      
04DF                             ; =============================================================================
04DF                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
04DF                             ; =============================================================================
04DF                          IF   CHECKED   
04DF                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
04DF                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
04DF                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
04DF                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
04DF                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
04DF                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile. DE is free between characters.
04DF   EB           CHKSTK:   EX   DE,HL   
04E0   21 05 F7               LD   HL,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
04E3   39                     ADD   HL,SP   
04E4   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
04E5   38 1D                  JR   C,e_under   
04E7   14                     INC   D   
04E8   20 16                  JR   NZ,e_over   
04EA   D9                     EXX      ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
04EB   7C                     LD   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
04EC   FE 07                  CP   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
04EE   7D                     LD   A,L   ;   page, in the guard band)
04EF   D9                     EXX      
04F0   20 0B                  JR   NZ,e_rover   
04F2   FE E1                  CP   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
04F4   D8                     RET   C   
04F5   D9                     EXX      ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
04F6   2E E0                  LD   L,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   (H is right: the pointer is in its page)
04F8   D9                     EXX      
04F9   3E 72                  LD   A,"r"   
04FB   18 48                  JR   errp   
04FD   3E 52        E_ROVER:   LD   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
04FF   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides the next entry)
0500   3E 53        E_OVER:   LD   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
0502   18 41                  JR   errp   
0504   31 FC 08     E_UNDER:   LD   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
0507   3E 73                  LD   A,"s"   
0509   18 54                  JR   error   
050B                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
050B                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a reserved one
050B                             ; in every build (AFh or C3h): if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of
050B                             ; an undefined word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
050B   04           E_HI:     INC   B   
050C   10 49                  DJNZ   e_resv   ; (B is as it was, and is not 0)
050E   CF                     RST   08h   
050F   42                     LD   B,D   
0510   4B                     LD   C,E   
0511   3E 55                  LD   A,"U"   
0513   18 4A                  JR   error   
0515                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the old one, the carry is from adding
0515                             ; the count. Stop if the top is not below the limit page, or is below the
0515                             ; program's end.
0515                CHKHP:       
0515                          ENDIF      
0515                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0515                             ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
0515                             ; range, so the add is tested too: growing (A, the count's high
0515                             ; byte, is positive) must not carry, and releasing must.
0515   1F                     RRA      ; the carry comes in above the sign:
0516   C6 40                  ADD   A,40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
0518   87                     ADD   A,A   
0519   38 10                  JR   C,e_heap   
051B   3A 07 00               LD   A,(0007h)   
051E   3D                     DEC   A   
051F   BC                     CP   H   
0520   38 09                  JR   C,e_heap   
0522                          ENDIF      
0522                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                                 ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
                                 ; round always falls outside it.)
                              LD   A,H   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              JR   NC,e_heap   
0522                          ENDIF      
0522                          IF   CHECKED   
0522   D5                     PUSH   DE   
0523   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0524   2A 38 09               LD   HL,(NPEND)   
0527   19                     ADD   HL,DE   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0528   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0529   D1                     POP   DE   
052A   D8                     RET   C   
052B   B7           E_HEAP:   OR   A   ; put the count back in TOS for the report
052C   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
052E   3E 48                  LD   A,"H"   
0530   18 13                  JR   errp   
0532                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0532                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0532                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0532                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0532                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0532                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0532                             ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
0532   23           CHKST:    INC   HL   
0533   7C                     LD   A,H   
0534   2B                     DEC   HL   
0535   FE 09                  CP   LETPAGE   
0537   38 07                  JR   C,e_store   
0539                          ENDIF      
0539                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
                              CP   HEAPLIM   
                              RET   C   
0539                          ENDIF      
0539                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
0539   5F                     LD   E,A   
053A   3A 07 00               LD   A,(0007h)   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
053D   3D                     DEC   A   
053E   BB                     CP   E   
053F   D0                     RET   NC   
0540                          ENDIF      
0540                          IF   CHECKED   
0540                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
0540                             ; a 3-byte LD DE,nn (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
0540   3E 4F        E_STORE:   LD   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
0542   11                     DB   11h   
0543   3E 42        E_BREAK:   LD   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
0545                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
0545   D1           ERRP:     POP   DE   
0546   18 17                  JR   error   
0548                             ; e_dollar: "$" ran into a NUL (in prstr): Q, with the string's address
0548                             ; back in TOS. prstr"s return address goes first. But if "$' had no
0548                             ; address at all (the stack was empty), it is s, found now: chkstk, called
0548                             ; one cell up, sees the stack past its empty place then.
0548   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   DE   
0549   E1                     POP   HL   
054A   CD DF 04               CALL   chkstk   
054D   E5                     PUSH   HL   
054E   2A 34 09               LD   HL,(RSAVE)   
0551   11                     DB   11h   ; (LD DE,nn hides e_quote's first two bytes)
0552   44           E_QUOTE:   LD   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
0553   4D                     LD   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
0554   3E 51                  LD   A,"Q"   
0556   11                     DB   11h   
0557   3E 58        E_RESV:   LD   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
0559   11                     DB   11h   
055A   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   LD   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
055C   11                     DB   11h   
055D   3E 57        E_BRACK:   LD   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
055F                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
055F                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
055F                             ; 
055F                             ;   Err X @ line,col
055F                             ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
055F                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
055F                             ;   Rtn n
055F   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   HL   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
0560   5F                     LD   E,A   
0561   CD 34 03               CALL   pnl   
0564   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
0569   7B                     LD   A,E   
056A   EF                     RST   28h   
056B   CD 3A 03               CALL   pmsg   
056E   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
0572   0B                     DEC   BC   ; BC = the place
0573                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
0573                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
0573                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
0573   21 80 09               LD   HL,LINEBUF   
0576   11 00 00               LD   DE,0   
0579   78                     LD   A,B   
057A   FE 0A                  CP   PROG/256   
057C   38 14                  JR   C,er3   
057E   24                     INC   H   
057F   6B                     LD   L,E   ; HL = PROG
0580   13           ER1:      INC   DE   ; a new line starts at HL
0581   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0582   7D           ER2:      LD   A,L   
0583   91                     SUB   C   
0584   7C                     LD   A,H   
0585   98                     SBC   A,B   
0586   30 09                  JR   NC,er2x   ; reached the place
0588   7E                     LD   A,(HL)   
0589   23                     INC   HL   
058A   FE 0A                  CP   10   
058C   20 F4                  JR   NZ,er2   
058E   F1                     POP   AF   
058F   18 EF                  JR   er1   
0591   E1           ER2X:     POP   HL   
0592   C5           ER3:      PUSH   BC   
0593   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0594   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0595   CD 54 04               CALL   pdec   ; the line
0598   3E 2C                  LD   A,","   
059A   EF                     RST   28h   
059B   D1                     POP   DE   
059C   E1                     POP   HL   
059D   E5                     PUSH   HL   
059E   B7                     OR   A   
059F   ED 52                  SBC   HL,DE   
05A1   23                     INC   HL   
05A2   CD 54 04               CALL   pdec   ; the column
05A5   CD 34 03               CALL   pnl   
05A8   22                     DB   22h   
05A9   E1                     POP   HL   ; the text, as it is: 16 characters, or fewer
05AA   06 10                  LD   B,16   ;   if the line or the program ends first
05AC   7E           ER4:      LD   A,(HL)   
05AD   23                     INC   HL   
05AE   B7                     OR   A   
05AF   28 0F                  JR   Z,er5   
05B1   FE 0D                  CP   13   
05B3   28 0B                  JR   Z,er5   
05B5   FE 0A                  CP   10   
05B7   28 07                  JR   Z,er5   
05B9                          ENDIF      
05B9                          IF   CHECKED*CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
05B9   FE 1A                  CP   1Ah   ; (the ^Z that pads a file's last record ends
05BB   28 03                  JR   Z,er5   ;   the text too: some terminals clear the
05BD                          ENDIF      ;   screen on it. The editor's loader ends
05BD                          IF   CHECKED   ;   the text at the first ^Z.)
05BD   EF                     RST   28h   
05BE   10 EC                  DJNZ   er4   
05C0                ER5:         ; (on into the two stack lines)
05C0                             ; The two stack lines:  Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
05C0                             ;                       Rtn n
05C0                             ; TOS is in memory with the rest (pushed) by now.
05C0   CD 34 03               CALL   pnl   
05C3   53 74 6B 20 22         DB   "Stk ",22h   
05C8   21 06 F7               LD   HL,(2-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; SP - (DSTOP-2) is minus twice the
05CB   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ;   depth (the cell at DSTOP-2 was pushed
05CC   E7                     RST   20h   ;   with the first value and holds nothing)
05CD   CD 14 06               CALL   phalf   ; the depth
05D0   3E 3A                  LD   A,":"   
05D2   EF                     RST   28h   
05D3   79                     LD   A,C   
05D4   FE 09                  CP   9   
05D6   38 0A                  JR   C,er6   
05D8   CD 3A 03               CALL   pmsg   
05DB   20 2E 2E 2E 22         DB   " ...",22h   
05E0   0E 08                  LD   C,8   
05E2   26 00        ER6:      LD   H,0   ; C = the number of cells to show
05E4   69                     LD   L,C   
05E5   29                     ADD   HL,HL   
05E6   39                     ADD   HL,SP   ; HL -> just above the deepest of them
05E7   0C                     INC   C   
05E8   0D           ER7:      DEC   C   
05E9   28 0F                  JR   Z,er8   
05EB   2B                     DEC   HL   
05EC   56                     LD   D,(HL)   
05ED   2B                     DEC   HL   
05EE   5E                     LD   E,(HL)   
05EF   E5                     PUSH   HL   
05F0   3E 20                  LD   A," "   
05F2   EF                     RST   28h   
05F3   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
05F4   CD 4C 04               CALL   psgn   
05F7   E1                     POP   HL   
05F8   18 EE                  JR   er7   
05FA   CD 34 03     ER8:      CALL   pnl   
05FD   52 74 6E 20 22         DB   "Rtn ",22h   
0602   D9                     EXX      ; RSTOP - HL' is under 256 (the pointer is
0603   3E E0                  LD   A,RSTOP&0FFh   ;   at most one entry below its page), so
0605   95                     SUB   L   ;   the low bytes are enough
0606   D9                     EXX      
0607   6F                     LD   L,A   
0608   26 00                  LD   H,0   
060A   CD 14 06               CALL   phalf   
060D   CD 34 03               CALL   pnl   
0610   22                     DB   22h   
0611                          ENDIF      
0611                          IF   CHECKED*(1-EDITOR)   
0611   C3 15 01               JP   endprog   
0614                          ENDIF      
0614                          IF   CHECKED*EDITOR   
                              JP   edit0   ; back to the editor, with both stacks cleared
0614                          ENDIF      
0614                          IF   CHECKED   
0614                             ; phalf: print half of HL, and leave it in C.
0614   CB 3C        PHALF:    SRL   H   
0616   CB 1D                  RR   L   
0618   E5                     PUSH   HL   
0619   CD 54 04               CALL   pdec   
061C   C1                     POP   BC   
061D   C9                     RET      
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                             ; =============================================================================
061E                             ;  The line editor (EDITOR = 1)
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  The interpreter starts here, and a program that ends comes back here.
061E                             ;  There is no prompt. It follows the spec's suggested standard for a line
061E                             ;  editor (docs/b8script.md, Environments). Type a line and press Return:
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;    n text    put the text in as line n; the lines from n on move down. A
061E                             ;              number past the end (or 0) adds the line at the end.
061E                             ;    n         take line n out
061E                             ;    anything else is run at once, as B8Script. (Start such a line with a
061E                             ;    space if it would begin with a digit.)
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  A command key ends the line too, and takes what was typed as its argument:
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;    ^G        run the program
061E                             ;    n ^L      list from line n (no number: all of it). Any key holds the
061E                             ;              list until another key is pressed; Ctrl-C ends it.
061E                             ;    n ^E      put line n in the input line; Return puts it back, changed
061E                             ;    name ^R   read. CP/M: the file of that name (no name: the same file as
061E                             ;              last time). Generic: what is typed, or pasted, from now until
061E                             ;              ^Z replaces the program; it is not echoed.
061E                             ;    name ^W   write. CP/M: to that file (no name: the same file as last
061E                             ;              time). Generic: the text is printed, as it is.
061E                             ;    ^N ^N     new: no program (the key twice in a row)
061E                             ;    ^X        leave (to LEAVE)
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  In the line: ^B and ^F, or the left and right arrow keys, move the cursor;
061E                             ;  a character goes in at the cursor; Backspace and DEL take out the one
061E                             ;  before it; Esc drops the line. Only CR, LF, BS and printing characters are
061E                             ;  sent to the terminal, so any terminal will do.
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  Lines are counted, not numbered: the text holds no line numbers, and the
061E                             ;  list shows each line's place. There can be 65535 lines. A typed line holds
061E                             ;  125 characters; the one character after a line number separates it from
061E                             ;  the text and is not stored. The text is kept as it is typed, each line
061E                             ;  ending in CR LF, at PROG.
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  What lasts from one line to the next: the program, the words, the
061E                             ;  variables and the data stack. An error or a break clears both stacks. The
061E                             ;  return stack starts empty for every line.
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  Things to know:
061E                             ;    - Reset empties the program (generic builds).
061E                             ;    - A word's address points into the program, so run the program again
061E                             ;      after editing it.
061E                             ;    - Nothing is printed between a program's output and what is typed next.
061E                             ;    - A line run at once sits in the line buffer, which -n? also reads into:
061E                             ;      a line that calls -n? and carries on afterwards runs what was typed.
061E                             ;      (The stored program never comes back to the line, so it may.)
061E                             ;    - The editor"s own keys are not the program"s: -n? is the plain line
061E                             ;      read of the other builds.
061E                             ; 
061E                             ;  The data stack is the CPU's stack, so the editor works on top of whatever
061E                             ;  the last line left there, with TOS pushed like the rest.
061E                             ; =============================================================================
061E                          IF   EDGEN   
                    INIT:        ; reset (A = 0)
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDGEN*CHECKED   
                                 ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at 0, and
                                 ; every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is caught at
                                 ; (see e_hi).
                              LD   HL,LET   
                    INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDGEN   
                              JR   edit0   
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR   
                                 ; ^F, right arrow: one to the right, by printing the character there
                    RIGHT:    LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the end
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   lf1   
                                 ; Esc: alone it drops the line. An arrow key sends Esc [ and a letter, so
                                 ; wait about 5 ms for a second key: after a "[" read on to the letter that
                                 ; ends the sequence, and act on C (right) and D (left).
                    ESC:      LD   BC,5*MSLOOP   
                    ES1:      CALL   rawk   
                              JR   NZ,es2   
                              DEC   BC   
                              LD   A,B   
                              OR   C   
                              JR   NZ,es1   
                              CALL   fin   ; no second key: the line is dropped
                              JR   edit   
                    ES2:      CP   "["   
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; not a sequence known here
                    ES3:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   40h   
                              JR   C,es3   ; (its parameters)
                              SUB   "C"   
                              JR   Z,right   
                              DEC   A   ; "D"?
                              JR   NZ,ed1   ; no: on into left
                                 ; ^B, left arrow: the cursor goes one to the left
                    LEFT:     LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; (L = 80h: at the start)
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                    LF1:      RST   28h   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; edit0: reset, an error or a break: both stacks are cleared, and the cursor
                                 ;   is shown, in case the program had hidden it and could not show it again.
                                 ; skend: a program that ended inside skip: its return address goes.
                                 ; edend: a program that ended: TOS joins the rest of the data stack.
                    EDIT0:    LD   SP,DSTOP-2   ; empty (the cell that stands for TOS is pushed)
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR*ANS   
                              XOR   A   ; (pshow wants the carry clear)
                              CALL   pshow   ; ESC [ ? 2 5 h
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR*(1-ANS)   
                              LD   A,1   
                              CALL   CONCUR   ; show the cursor
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR   
                              DB   21h   ; (LD HL,nn: steps over the next two bytes)
                    SKEND:    POP   DE   
                    EDEND:    PUSH   HL   
                                 ; edit: start a new input line.
                    EDIT:     EXX      
                              LD   HL,RSTOP   ; the return stack is empty
                              EXX      
                              LD   HL,0   
                              LD   (KEYBUF),HL   ; no key is held, and the break key is on
                              LD   (EDLN),HL   ; no line is being edited
                              LD   HL,LINEBUF   ; HL = the cursor,
                              LD   E,L   ;   E = the end of the line (its low byte)
                    ED1:      CALL   ekey   
                              CP   7Fh   
                              JR   Z,bsp   ; DEL
                              CP   " "   
                              JR   NC,insc   
                              CP   9   
                              JR   Z,insc   ; Tab is text
                              CP   8   
                              JR   Z,bsp   
                              CP   2   
                              JR   Z,left   ; ^B
                              CP   6   
                              JR   Z,right   ; ^F
                              CP   1Bh   
                              JR   Z,esc   
                              PUSH   HL   ; a command key? Look it up
                              LD   HL,cmds   
                              LD   B,NCMD   
                    ED2:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,ed3   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   ed2   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ed1   ; no: the key is ignored
                    ED3:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   H,(HL)   
                              LD   L,A   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; the command's address: fin returns to it
                                 ; fin: end the input line: CR LF and a NUL after it, and a new line on the
                                 ; terminal. Leaves BC -> the line and HL -> the NUL.
                    FIN:      LD   H,LETPAGE   
                              LD   L,E   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              DEC   L   
                              CALL   prl   ; (prints the CR LF)
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              LD   BC,LINEBUF   
                              RET      
                                 ; Backspace, DEL: the character before the cursor goes. The cursor moves
                                 ; left, the rest of the line moves down over it, and the last place (now a
                                 ; space) is printed over along with the rest.
                    BSP:      LD   A,L   
                              ADD   A,A   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; at the start
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    BS1:      INC   L   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              LD   A,L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,bs1   
                              DEC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   D,E   
                              DEC   E   
                              JR   ic2   
                                 ; A character goes in at the cursor: it ripples up through the rest of the
                                 ; line, the cursor moves on, and the rest is printed again.
                    INSC:     LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   
                              JR   Z,ed1   ; the line is full: 125 characters
                              LD   A,B   
                              RST   28h   
                              PUSH   HL   
                    IC1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (HL),B   
                              LD   B,A   
                              LD   A,L   
                              INC   L   
                              CP   E   
                              JR   NZ,ic1   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   L   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   D,E   
                    IC2:      CALL   tail   
                              JR   ed1   
                                 ; tail: print the line from the cursor to D (a low byte), and bring the
                                 ; cursor back with backspaces. Nothing at all if the cursor is at D.
                    TAIL:     LD   C,L   
                    TA1:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   D   
                              JR   Z,ta2   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   ta1   
                    TA2:      LD   A,L   
                              CP   C   
                              RET   Z   
                              LD   A,8   
                              RST   28h   
                              DEC   L   
                              JR   ta2   
                                 ; ekey: wait for a key
                    EKEY:     CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,ekey   
                              RET      
                                 ; The command keys, and where each goes (after fin).
                    CMDS:     DB   13   
                              DW   cret   
                              DB   7   ; ^G
                              DW   crun   
                              DB   12   ; ^L
                              DW   clist   
                              DB   5   ; ^E
                              DW   cedln   
                              DB   18   ; ^R
                              DW   cread   
                              DB   23   ; ^W
                              DW   cwrite   
                              DB   14   ; ^N
                              DW   cnew   
                              DB   24   ; ^X
                              DW   LEAVE   
                    NCMD:     EQU   8   
                                 ; ^N ^N: no program, if the next key is ^N too
                    CNEW:     CALL   ekey   
                              CP   14   
                              JR   NZ,ged0   
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   (PROG),A   
                    GED0:     JP   edit   
                                 ; ^E: line n goes into the input line, to be changed. EDLN remembers which
                                 ; line it was: Return puts the text back in its place.
                    CEDLN:    CALL   rdnum   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   ; HL -> the line, or the NUL if there is none
                              POP   DE   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged0   
                              LD   (EDLN),DE   
                              LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                    CE1:      LD   A,(HL)   ; copy it, and show it, up to its CR (or LF)
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,ce2   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   E   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   0FDh   ; (a longer line is cut at 125 characters)
                              JR   NZ,ce1   
                    CE2:      EX   DE,HL   ; the cursor is at the line's end
                              LD   E,L   
                              JP   ed1   
                                 ; Return. If ^E put a line here, the text goes back in its place. If not:
                                 ; a number and text is a line to put in, a number alone a line to take out,
                                 ; and anything else is run where it is.
                    CRET:     PUSH   HL   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   HL,(EDLN)   
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   Z,cr1   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   delln   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   ins   
                    CR1:      CALL   rdnum   ; HL = the number it starts with, BC -> after
                              LD   A,C   ; C is still 80h if there was no number:
                              ADD   A,A   ;   only then is twice it 0
                              JR   Z,st0p   ; no number: run the line
                              LD   A,(BC)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,cr2   
                              POP   DE   ; the number alone: take that line out
                              CALL   delln   
                              JR   gedit   
                    CR2:      INC   BC   ; step over the one character after the number
                                 ; Put the text at BC in as line n (in HL): open a gap of its length there,
                                 ; CR and LF included, and copy it in.
                    INS:      CALL   find   ; HL -> where it goes
                              POP   DE   ; the end of what was typed
                              LD   A,E   
                              SUB   C   ; A = the length of the text, with its CR LF
                              PUSH   BC   ; the text
                              LD   C,A   
                              LD   B,0   
                              PUSH   BC   ; its length
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   ; DE = where it goes
                              XOR   A   
                              LD   C,A   ; BC = 0: CPIR looks as far as it needs to
                              CPIR      ; HL -> one past the program's NUL
                              SBC   HL,DE   ; the number of bytes to move up, NUL included
                              LD   B,H   
                              LD   C,L   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              EX   (SP),HL   ; HL = the length; where it goes is kept
                              PUSH   HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   ; the NUL's new place
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              LDDR      ; move the rest of the program up
                              POP   BC   ; the length
                              POP   DE   ; where it goes
                              POP   HL   ; the text
                              LDIR      
                    GEDIT:    JP   edit   
                                 ; ^G: run the program. st0p: run the typed line (BC -> it).
                    CRUN:     LD   BC,PROG   
                              DB   3Eh   ; (LD A,n: steps over the POP)
                    ST0P:     POP   HL   ; (the end of what was typed)
                                 ; st0: start running at BC. The heap starts after the stored program's NUL.
                    ST0:      LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    ST1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,st1   
                              LD   (HEAP),HL   
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR*CHECKED   
                              RST   20h   ; minus the heap"s first address: "_' may not
                              LD   (NPEND),HL   ;   release below it
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR   
                              POP   HL   ; TOS: the data stack is as the last line left it
                              RST   30h   ; (its return address is thrown away)
                                 ; ^L: list from line n. DE = the number of the line at HL.
                    CLIST:    CALL   rdnum   ; HL = n, or 0 if there was none:
                              LD   A,H   
                              OR   L   
                              JR   NZ,li0   
                              INC   L   ;   then from line 1
                    LI0:      PUSH   HL   
                              CALL   find   
                              POP   DE   
                    LI1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; the end of the text
                              CALL   rawk   
                              JR   Z,li3   ; no key: carry on
                              CP   3   
                              CALL   NZ,ekey   ; any key but Ctrl-C: wait for one more
                              CP   3   
                              JR   Z,gedit   ; Ctrl-C, first or second, ends the list
                    LI3:      PUSH   HL   
                              PUSH   DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              CALL   pdec   ; the line's number,
                              LD   A," "   
                              RST   28h   ;   a space,
                              POP   DE   
                              POP   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              CALL   prl   ;   and the line
                              JR   li1   
                                 ; delln: take line n (in HL) out: copy everything after it down over it.
                    DELLN:    CALL   find   
                              LD   D,H   
                              LD   E,L   
                              CALL   nxl   ; HL -> the next line
                    DE1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              LD   (DE),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              INC   DE   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   NZ,de1   
                              RET      
                                 ; find: HL = a line number. Returns HL -> that line, or -> the NUL at the end
                                 ; of the text if there are fewer lines (or the number is 0). Keeps BC.
                    FIND:     EX   DE,HL   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                    FI1:      DEC   DE   
                              LD   A,D   
                              OR   E   
                              RET   Z   
                              CALL   nxl   
                              JR   NZ,fi1   
                              RET      
                                 ; nxl: step HL over one line, to just past its LF (and return not-zero), or
                                 ; stop at the NUL that ends the text (and return zero).
                    NXL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              RET   Z   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,nxl   
                              OR   A   
                              RET      
                                 ; prl: print the line at HL, to its LF; HL -> just past it.
                    PRL:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              RST   28h   
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,prl   
                              RET      
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDGEN   
                    GED1:     JP   edit   
                                 ; ^R, generic: what comes in from now until ^Z is the program. A CR is
                                 ; stored as CR LF; a LF right after a line end is dropped (it is the CR's
                                 ; own, or an empty line's), and a LF anywhere else ends a line too. A last
                                 ; line with no end is given one. Nothing is echoed, and there is no check
                                 ; for running out of memory.
                    CREAD:    LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; (as if a line had just ended: the byte is
                              INC   HL   ;   the line buffer's last, and spare)
                    RD1:      CALL   ekey   
                              LD   C,A   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd2   
                              LD   A,10   ; ^Z ends the last line, as a LF would
                    RD2:      CP   10   
                              JR   NZ,rd3   
                              DEC   HL   
                              CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   Z,rd4   ; straight after a line end: dropped
                              LD   A,13   ; anywhere else it ends the line
                    RD3:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   HL   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   NZ,rd4   
                              LD   (HL),10   ; after a CR goes a LF
                              INC   HL   
                    RD4:      LD   A,C   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,rd1   
                              LD   (HL),0   
                              JR   ged1   
                                 ; ^W, generic: the text is printed as it is, for the terminal to capture.
                    CWRITE:   LD   HL,PROG   
                    CW1:      LD   A,(HL)   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ged1   
                              RST   28h   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   cw1   
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   EDITOR*CPM   
                    CFCB:     EQU   005Ch   ; the file's name is kept here, where the CCP
                                 ;   put the one from the command line
                                 ; ^R, CP/M: read the file. A name typed before the key is the file's name
                                 ; from now on.
                    CREAD:    CALL   setname   
                              CALL   load   
                              JP   edit   
                                 ; ^W, CP/M: write the file: delete the old one, make it anew, write the
                                 ; text in records of 128 bytes, and close it. The text's NUL and the 127
                                 ; bytes after it are set to ^Z meanwhile, which pads the last record. (A
                                 ; full disk or directory is not noticed: the calls fail and that is all.)
                    CWRITE:   CALL   setname   
                              LD   C,19   ; delete
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   C,22   ; make
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              LD   HL,PROG   
                              XOR   A   
                    CW1:      CP   (HL)   
                              INC   HL   
                              JR   NZ,cw1   
                              DEC   HL   ; HL -> the NUL
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   B,128   
                    CW2:      LD   (HL),1Ah   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   cw2   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    CW3:      LD   A,E   ; a record that starts before the end is written
                              SUB   L   
                              LD   A,D   
                              SBC   A,H   
                              JR   NC,cw4   
                              PUSH   HL   
                              LD   C,21   ; write, from where the record lies
                              CALL   frec   
                              POP   HL   
                              JR   cw3   
                    CW4:      LD   (HL),0   ; the NUL again
                              LD   C,16   ; close
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              JP   edit   
                                 ; frec: BDOS function C (read or write a record) with the 128 bytes at DE.
                                 ; Returns A = the BDOS's answer, HL = DE and DE = DE + 128.
                    FREC:     PUSH   DE   
                              PUSH   BC   
                              LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   BC   
                              CALL   fbdos   
                              POP   HL   
                              LD   DE,128   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              ADD   HL,DE   
                              EX   DE,HL   
                              RET      
                                 ; setname: if a name was typed (the line does not start with its CR), put it
                                 ; in the FCB: up to 8 characters, a dot, up to 3 more, in capitals. The drive
                                 ; is the current one. Then, name or no name, clear the FCB after the name,
                                 ; as it must be before a file is opened or made.
                    SETNAME:   LD   DE,LINEBUF   
                              LD   A,(DE)   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              LD   HL,CFCB   
                              LD   (HL),0   ; the current drive
                              LD   B,11   
                    SN1:      INC   L   
                              LD   (HL)," "   
                              DJNZ   sn1   
                              LD   L,CFCB+1   
                    SN2:      LD   A,(DE)   
                              INC   DE   
                              CP   13   
                              JR   Z,fcbclr   
                              CP   "."   
                              JR   NZ,sn3   
                              LD   L,CFCB+9   ; the type
                              JR   sn2   
                    SN3:      CP   "a"   
                              JR   C,sn4   
                              AND   5Fh   ; a capital
                    SN4:      LD   (HL),A   
                              INC   L   
                              JR   sn2   
                    FCBCLR:   LD   HL,CFCB+12   
                              LD   B,24   
                    FC1:      LD   (HL),0   
                              INC   HL   
                              DJNZ   fc1   
                              RET      
                                 ; fbdos: BDOS function C on the file
                    FBDOS:    LD   DE,CFCB   
                              JP   BDOS   
                                 ; load: read the file into PROG. No such file: no program. The text ends at
                                 ; the file"s first ^Z (1Ah), which pads a text file"s last record; one more
                                 ; goes after the last record, so the search always stops. And every line
                                 ; must end in LF: a last line without one is given a CR LF. (The FCB is
                                 ; clear after its name: the CCP left it so, or setname did.)
                    LOAD:     LD   C,15   ; open (no such file: the first read fails
                              CALL   fbdos   ;   too)
                              LD   DE,PROG   
                    LD1:      LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
                              CALL   frec   
                              OR   A   
                              JR   Z,ld1   
                              LD   (HL),1Ah   ; (HL = where the record that failed would be)
                              LD   HL,PROG-1   
                              LD   A,10   ; (a file with no text needs nothing added)
                    TR1:      INC   HL   
                              LD   E,A   ; E = the character before this one
                              LD   A,(HL)   
                              CP   1Ah   
                              JR   NZ,tr1   
                              LD   A,E   
                              CP   10   
                              JR   Z,tr2   
                              LD   (HL),13   
                              INC   HL   
                              LD   (HL),10   
                              INC   HL   
                    TR2:      LD   (HL),0   
                              RET      
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                             ; =============================================================================
061E                          IF   CPM   
061E                             ; The RAM pages follow the image; the heap may grow to the BDOS.
061E                START:       
061E                          ENDIF      
061E                          IF   CPM*CHECKED   
061E                             ; Clear the lower half of the letter page: every variable starts at
061E                             ; 0, every word cell holds 0000h, the address an undefined word is
061E                             ; caught at (see e_hi: the byte there is CP/M's JP, C3h), and no key
061E                             ; is held back.
061E   21 00 09               LD   HL,LET   
0621   AF                     XOR   A   
0622   77           INI1:     LD   (HL),A   
0623   2C                     INC   L   
0624   F2 22 06               JP   P,ini1   ; +00h to +7Fh
0627                          ENDIF      
0627                          IF   CPM   
0627   21 08 01               LD   HL,vecs   ; the RST routines go down into page zero
062A   11 08 00               LD   DE,0008h   
062D   01 2C 00               LD   BC,vecend-vecs   
0630   ED B0                  LDIR      
0632                          ENDIF      
0632                          IF   CPM*EDITOR   
                              CALL   load   ; the file named on the command line
                              JP   edit0   
0632                          ENDIF      
0632                          IF   CPM*(1-EDITOR)   
0632   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   ; open the file named on the command line
0635   0E 0F                  LD   C,15   ; (no such file: the first read fails too,
0637   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   ;   and the program is empty)
063A   11 00 0A               LD   DE,PROG   
063D   D5           LD1:      PUSH   DE   
063E   0E 1A                  LD   C,26   ; set the DMA address
0640   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
0643   11 5C 00               LD   DE,005Ch   
0646   0E 14                  LD   C,20   ; read the next 128 bytes
0648   CD 05 00               CALL   BDOS   
064B   E1                     POP   HL   ; HL = the address this record went to
064C   B7                     OR   A   
064D   20 07                  JR   NZ,ld2   
064F   11 80 00               LD   DE,128   
0652   19                     ADD   HL,DE   
0653   EB                     EX   DE,HL   
0654   18 E7                  JR   ld1   
0656   36 00        LD2:      LD   (HL),0   ; the end of the file counts as NUL
0658   23                     INC   HL   ; the heap starts after it
0659   01 00 0A               LD   BC,PROG   ; the IP
065C   C3 76 01               JP   st2   
065F                          ENDIF      
065F                          IF   CPM   
065F                             ; RAM pages, after the image
065F                RSPAGE:   EQU   (imgend + 255) / 256   
065F                DSPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 1   
065F                LETPAGE:   EQU   RSPAGE + 2   
065F                PROG:     EQU   LETPAGE*256 + 256   
065F                          ENDIF      
065F                IMGEND:      


